ght be the  safest approach all of our students will  be tested before they show up  upon arrival and during the quarantine  toward the end  so we will know at the end of those 14  days that  any student coming out will have had  three negative tests  within a normal period in which the  disease exhibits itself  awesome it's a secluded community  alex didn't have a chance to return home  to vietnam when covet 19 closed the  school in the spring  the international student has been  living on campus ever since  and supports the quarantine what do you  say to other students  who are fearful in coming back to campus  i think uh the fear is totally valid i  myself am very nervous about  everyone coming back how risky do you  feel it is for you to be on campus  i actually think it's less risky for me  to be on campus rather than returning  home  marianna lemon is willing to make  sacrifices  for the on-campus experience the  freshmen from the bronx  moved in over the summer i still want to  have a freshman year and i'm still here  and i'm like honestly willing to like  always be in my room and just take  classes  online from my room and only talk to my  roommate and maybe  have like the social distance lunches or  dinners kind of deals outside when it's  still warm  out so i'm willing to like have like a  alternate  freshman year if that's what it takes  the students we spoke with  admit the lack of socializing will be  difficult when you're apart you're not  building that kind of connection that  you would have when you're here  especially for a linebacker on the  school's football team  aj desantis says team building is the  point  that's one of the most important things  in football because it's not one guy in  the field at that time it's many guys on  the field guys working together special  teams offense defense everything  together  if there's one thing we've seen  nationwide from georgia tech to the  university of north carolina at chapel  hill and usc  it's that college students will still  socialize in large groups  despite the risk leading those campuses  to either  shut down or quarantine infected  students  casey has a plan for that too we're  doing waste  water testing the virus exhibits itself  in wastewater often before you see it in  your mucus  or or your blood really yes so we have  put  readers wastewater readers on all of our  residence halls  all of the houses on broad street where  a lot of our students live  so if we detect any increase  in the virus which you'll see first in  wastewater we will immediately test  everyone in that particular house how  much is it costing you to do that  millions of dollars  we purchased a hotel so we have a  quarantine  site millions in the singular or we  approaching  10 million we are below 10 million three  rounds of testing  rapid testing machines all of our dining  halls had to be completely retrofitted  to  grab and go extra staff to do the  testing  you know we're north of four million  dollars right now that's a lot of money  just  out of out of pocket so you want this to  work i want this to work  so much so president casey is currently  living in a dorm room himself  neighboring his students for 17 days if  i'm asking you to do this  i'll do it too so whatever food you're  eating i'm going to eat whatever rules  you have about when you're allowed  outside that's when i'll go outside so  i'm doing it with them  no special treatment are we supposed to  believe that i'm the college president  the fact that i have a single known  bathroom strikes people is a real real  plus  and the president's r.a alex he'll be  staying in  my floor in my building so it's a lucky  coincidence  are you going to lay down the law if you  see the president break the rules  yes i am not afraid to have that  conversation  okay we will be following up okay  casey acknowledges the living situation  he's asking students to go through  isn't ideal but in our new world he says  it's essential why i